  "caveats": [
    "Coverage is marginal over the whole test fold; ligand-grouped CV makes it a new-ligand coverage statement, not a new-paper one. MSRS-7 tests the paper split.",
    "The difficulty model is fitted on inner-OOF residuals from the proper-train ligands only, so it never sees calibration or test rows. It is still a learned quantity and can be optimistic where a ligand is unlike anything in training.",
    "The actionable set is defined on matched pairs (loose key). A pair is actionable only if both endpoints' intervals are narrow; this is conservative.",
    "Metal-conditional quantiles fall back to the global quantile when a metal has fewer than 30 calibration rows, which is the case for Rh/Os in several folds.",
    "The actionable-vs-rest contrast resamples DOIs and re-selects the actionable set inside each resample, so the CI includes selection variability."
  ]
